    anlanote = {Agentivity and Causation: Data from Hare"This paper represents part of an investigation into thenature of agentivity and its status as a universal syntacticand semantic category. We will investigate certain semanticrestrictions on eligibility for subject of a transitive verbin Hare, a Mackenzie Valley Athapaskan language, and thesemantic significance of the grammatical mechanism used toattribute causal function to one class of quasi-agents whichare ineligible for transitive subject status. Finally I willsuggest that these data constitute evidence for a multifactoral prototype definition of transitivity."ca.12},
