    anlanote = {Ms. 18 files of Menovschikov's notebooks. All in Russian.G. A. Menovshchikov worked with the four varieties of Eskimo spoken in Siberia during Soviet times: Central Siberian Yupik (from the Chokotak side, called Chaplinsky), Naukan Yupik, Sirenik Eskimo, and Bering Strait Inupiaq (Big Diomede). His work includes collecting, editing and translating texts; composing dictionaries and other lexicons; grammatical investigations culminating in a number of grammar books for various audiences (native, non-native, linguists), and writing, in Russian, various accounts of Eskimo culture and life in general aimed at the common reader. He also did considerable work on comparative Eskimo, and pedagogy directed at Soviet Eskimo children},
