    title = {A collection of Anthony Woodburys published papers},
    year = {1970},
    url = {http://www.uaf.edu/anla/item.xml?id=CY978W1970},
    anlanote = {Ts. Off-prints of papers published by A. Woodbury 1977-1996. Collected by Steven Jacobson. See also a collection of notes and correspondence CY978W1970b.f.1 Stridentization of Voiced Continuants in Dialects of Central Yup'ik Eskimo, 1979.f.2 Switch Reference, Syntactic Organization and Rhetorical Structure in Central Yup'ik Eskimo, 1982.f.3 The Functions of Rhetorical Structure: Some current issues, and a discussion of Central Alaskan Yup'ik narrative and conversation, 1983.f.4 [Book Review] Cev'armiut Qanemciit Qulirait-llu: Eskimo Narratives and Tales from Chevak, Alaska, 1985.f.5 Meaningful Phonological Process: A consideration of Central Alaskan Yup'ik Eskimo prosody, 1984.f.6 Intonation Without Moveable Stress in Central Alaskan Yup'ik, 1985.f.7 Rhetorical Structure in a Central Alaskan Yup'ik Eskimo Traditional Narrative, 1985.f.8 Marginal Agent Clauses in Central Alaskan Yup'ik Eskimo Internal and External Syntax, 1985.f.9 Noun, Nominal Sentence, and Clause in Central Alaskan Yup'ik Eskimo, 1985.f.10 Phrasing and Intonational Tonology in Central Alaskan Yup'ik Eskimo: Some implications for linguistics in the field, 1989.f.11 Utterance-final Phonology and the Prosodic Hierarchy: A case from the Nunivak dialect of Central Alaskan Yup'ik Eskimo, 1992.f.12 A Defense of the Proposition, 'When a language Dies, a Culture Dies', 1993.f.13 The Poetics and Rhetoric of Conversational Overlap in a Sample of Yup'ik Men's House Speech, 1995.f.14 Documenting Rhetorical, Aesthetic and Expressive Loss in Language Shift,1996},
    anlclanguage = {Yup'ik-Central-Alaskan},
    anlctype = {description},
    citation = {Papers published in various academic journals},
    comments = {A decision was made to keep these papers together under one identifier. Note that the identifier does not reflect the published date for any of these papers but is meant to represent the earliest decade of the publications},
    format = {Text},
    glottolog_ref_id = {168237},
    lgcode = {Yup'ik-Central-Alaskan}
}
