    anlanote = {Photocopies.Documents work done on place names of northwestern Alaska. Various documents appear to have gotten mixed up but this is a pretty complete description of what is in the folder.1. Unaliq place names, Nome 1981, with Robert Appok and Mark Abloogalook.2. Place names collected by Kaplan and others at Elders' Conference in Nome, summer 1981.3. Golovin place names, collected by Kaplan from Helen Amaktoolik at Bering Straits Elders' Conference, 1979 [Unaliq dialect of Central Yupik and Fish River dialect of Inupiaq].4. Wales place names, transcribed by Kaplan.5. Unalakleet place names from 1980 Nome Elders' Conference [includes some Central Yupik names].6. Place names for Koyukuk area collected at Nome Elders' Conference April 2, 1980 by Kaplan.7. Place names north of St. Michael provided by Archie Atchak (Aqupak -I), Nome Elders' Conference 1983, transcribed by Kaplan.8. Shaktoolik place names provided by John Auliye, collected and transcribed by Kaplan, Nome Elders' Conference, 1983.9. Unalakleet place names provided by Wassily Ekon and Henry Nashalook, transcribed by Kaplan, Nome Elders' Conference.10. White Mountain place names provided by Agnes Komakhuk, checked by Kaplan.11. Council place names collected by Agnes Komakhuk, checked by Kaplan.12. Teller and Mary's Igloo place names collected at Nome Elders' Conference, April 1, 1979. Transcribed by Kaplan.13. Golovin place names collected by Agnes Komakhuk, checked by Kaplan.14. Brevig Mission place names collected by Annie Olanna, Inupiaq by Kaplan.15. Golovin area place names given by Tommy Punguk, Inupiaq speaker; collected on tape by Jim Magadanz, transcribed in Eskimo by Kaplan.16. Golovin area place names given by Katherine Olson, speaker of Unaliq Central Yupik. Collected on tape by Jim Magadanz, Fish and Game, Nome. Transcribed in Eskimo by Kaplan. All names are written in CY orthography except those marked. Names in this area may be in either language and some are hybrids of both.17. Golovin area place names given by Florence Willoya, Fish River Inupiaq, collected by Magadanz, transcribed by Kaplan.18. Places named by Verne Eutuk, Serge Obruk and ALfred Olanna.19. Map by Magadanz},
