    title = {Tlingit language mss., not located},
    year = {1855},
    url = {http://www.uaf.edu/anla/item.xml?id=TL855N1855b},
    anlanote = {Two lists or accounts: (1.a) James C. Pilling, "Proof Sheets of a Bibliography of the Languages of the American Indians," 1885:527 (B885.P1885), (b) earlier in William H. Dall and Marcus Baker, "Pacific Coast Pilot," U.S. Coast and Geodetic Survey 1879:284, from "Otchet Rossiysko-Amerikanskoy Kompanii…", St. Petersburg, 1863, Vol. ii, table v; (c) also ms. English translation, Bancroft Collection, report by Kostlivstov; (d) original, not seen. (A.1) The gospel according to Matthew, 2, the Liturgy, 3, Doxologies and hymns for eight voices, 4, Canticle and short hymn for Pentecost Week, 5, Apostol v nedeliu 30 zach. 258, 6, The Gospel for Easter; (B) eight prayers and hymns for vesper services (names listed); (c) conversational vocabulary, 1, topical list (topics listed, e.g. flora-fauna), 2, numerals (cardinal, ordinal, fractions), 3, alphabetical Russian-Tlingit vocabulary; examples of invariable parts of speech.(2) P. A. Tikhmenev, "Istoricheskoe Obozrenie…1861-1863," English translation by Richard A. Pierce and Alton S. Donnelly, "History of the Russian-American Company," Seattle: University of Washington Press, 1978:387-388: "At present the Kolosh had many prayers, the mass, the gospels of St. Matthew and St. John, and the ten commandments translated in their language. Besides this many words and sentences used in conversation have been printed in alphabetical order."Date approximate. Much of the liturgical material is in the publication TL855.N1896, also John 1:1-17. The Gospel of Matthew is TL855.N1855 (which includes also the Decalogue). The Bancroft Collection ms. (Pinart copy), catalogued TL850.An1873, is no doubt Nadezhdin, including John 1:1-17 and the conversational sentences. However, the Gospel of John (if more complete than 1:1-17) is missing, and above all the alphabetical lexicon. The topical lexicon and examples of invariable parts of speech have been found in the Vinokurov Collection, Alaska State Historical Library},
    anlclanguage = {Tlingit},
    anlctype = {lexicon, text-religious},
    format = {Text},
    glottolog_ref_id = {172561},
    lgcode = {Tlingit [tli]}
}
