    year = {1862-1983},
    url = {http://www.uaf.edu/anla/item.xml?id=TS862M1862},
    anlanote = {A collection of articles concerning Missionary Influences on the Tsimshian People of Alaska and Canada; Various authors and dates- Tomorrow is Growing Old: "The Minthorns at Metlakatla" by Arthur O. Roberts (1978)- Northwest Languages Newsletter, Listing of Tlingit workshops planned for Native Language (Jan. 1983)- "William Duncan and the Genesis of Metlakatla" in Alaska/magazine of life on the last frontier (Feb. 1972)- The history of the Church missionary Society, Volume 3: "The Red Indian Missions: Patterns of Zeal and Triumphs of Grace" see pp.629 (1899)- "William Duncan; Founder and Developer of Alaska's Metlakatla Christian Mission" by Edward D. Kohlstedt (1957)- "Contact and Conflict: Indo-European Relations in British Columbia, 1774-1890" by Robin Fisher. pp.28-31, 46-47, 124-145, 204-207 (Sept. 1992)- The British Pacific. pp.65-75, see pp.68 (1902)- "McCullagh of Aiyansh" by J.W.W. Moeran, M.A. pp.5-7, 41-49, 206-209 (1923)- Chapter XXXVII "The British Columbia Mission" in Story of the Church Missionary Society IV. by Eugene Stock (1916) see pp.382-389, "A Transformed People," see pp.510-513 "The Far West: The Church Among Red Indians" see pp.237-253. "Story of Metlakahtla" by Mr. W. Duncan, pp.522-533 See above citation, - "An Appeal from Bishop Ridley," "The New Diocese of Caledonia," "The Prayer of the Drowning Indians" in The Church Missionary Gleaner pp.98-99 (unsure of year and volume, est. 1879-1890 era)- "Historical Sketches, Caledonia and its First Bishop" in the Canadian Church Magazine (Nov. 1887) Vol.1 No. 17- Senator MacDonald's misleading account of his Visit to Metlakatla Exposed by the Bishop of Caledonia pp.1-12 (1882)- William Duncan of Metlakatla: A Victorian Missionary in British Columbia by Jean Usher. National Museum of Man, Ottawa, Canada (1974)- The Apostle of Alaska: The Story of William Duncan of Metlakahtla by John W. Arctander, LL.D pp.56-59, 338-345, 363-365 (1909)- "Red Indians I have Known: A Word to the Reader" (Ridley? date unknown, est. early 1900's era) pp.2-29- "News from Kincolitii" 4 Damaged pages. Publisher and date unknown- "Stranger than Fiction" various chapters. by J.J. Halcombe pp.240-255, 289-305, 353-366, 417-496, 579-586, 609-620, 673-677 (Dec 1871) - "A Contrast" by W. Duncan. pp.195-205 (Sept 1863)- "Recent Intelligence" in Church Missionary Intelligencer (extracted from letter written by Mr. W. Duncan (Sept. 1, 1862) 2 damaged pages- "Ch. XIII An Apostle of Alaska" in Up and Down the North Pacific Coast by Canoe and Mission Ship by Rev. Thomas Crosby, D.D. pp.165-167 (1914)- Metlakahtla: A True Narrative of the Red Man by George T.B. Davis (1904)- Heroes of the Church in British Columbia: Special Missionary Lessons, Epiphany, 1958. Diocese of New Westminster, Board of Religious Education. pp.1-67},
